# === Calibration lookup tables: runtime output, NOT versioned ===
# Calibration.py rewrites these on every peak-detection run and they are
# per-device (100001 lines each), so versioning them buried every diff under
# ~400k lines of churn that says nothing about the code. main still tracks them;
# this branch does not, so expect a .gitignore conflict on the next merge.
#
# ⚠️ Consequence: a fresh clone has no calibration table. Run Peak Detection once
#    before Single / Multiscan / Raw Data — those paths loadtxt() the file with no
#    fallback and will raise if it is missing.
#
# Still versioned: PeakFrequencies{,RT}.txt (a handful of lines, no churn) and
# sweep_data/*.txt (example spectra the Raw Data and Conductance views read).
software/openQCM/Calibration_5MHz.txt
software/openQCM/Calibration_10MHz.txt

